> **Role:** Senior Data & Full-Stack Systems Architect.
> **Task:** Build an automated Government Scheme Ingestion, Embedding, RAG Retrieval, and Application Generation Pipeline for a Women Founders Funding Platform.
> **Tech Stack:** React.js (Tailwind CSS), Node.js, Express, MongoDB (Mongoose), `faiss-node` (Local Vector Database), `pdf-parse`, Gemini API (`text-embedding-004` & Gemini Pro/Flash).
> 
> ---
> 
> ### PART 1: DEVELOPER MANUAL SETUP CHECKLIST (Prerequisites)
> *Before executing the automated code scripts, the developer must perform these 5 manual steps:*
> 
> 1. **Directory Setup:**
>    Create the following folder structure in the Node.js project root:
>    ```text
>    project-root/
>    ├── data/
>    │   ├── pdfs/           <-- Place downloaded scheme PDFs here
>    │   └── vectors/        <-- faiss-node index binary & mapping will be generated here
>    ├── models/
>    │   ├── Scheme.js       <-- MongoDB Schema for Schemes
>    │   └── Application.js  <-- MongoDB Schema for User Applications
>    ├── scripts/
>    │   └── seedSchemes.js  <-- Data Extraction, Vectorization & Seeding Script
>    ├── utils/
>    │   └── schemeMatcher.js<-- Hybrid RAG Search Utility
>    └── controllers/
>        └── schemeController.js <-- Express Request Handlers
>    ```
> 
> 2. **Document Acquisition (PDF Downloads):**
>    Download official guidelines PDFs for women-centric government schemes and place them into `./data/pdfs/`:
>    - `standup_india.pdf` (from `standupmitra.in`)
>    - `mudra_pmmy.pdf` (from `mudra.org.in`)
>    - `cgtmse_women.pdf` (from `cgtmse.in`)
>    - `tread_scheme.pdf` (from `msme.gov.in` / `myscheme.gov.in`)
> 
> 3. **Package Installation:**
>    Run this terminal command:
>    `npm install pdf-parse faiss-node @google/generative-ai mongoose dotenv express cors`
> 
> 4. **Environment Variables Config:**
>    Ensure `.env` contains:
>    ```env
>    MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
>    GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key
>    PORT=5000
>    ```
> 
> 5. **Execution Command:**
>    After code generation, run `node scripts/seedSchemes.js` from the root terminal to populate MongoDB and create local vector binaries.
> 
