> 
> ### PART 2: AUTOMATED CODE IMPLEMENTATION SPECIFICATIONS
> 
> Generate complete, production-grade, error-handled code for the following modules:
> 
> #### 1. Mongoose Schemas
> - **`models/Scheme.js`:**
>   - `schemeName` (String, required, unique)
>   - `category` (String, e.g., "Loan", "Grant", "Subsidy")
>   - `minWomenOwnership` (Number, default: 51) // % female equity required
>   - `maxLoanAmount` (Number) // INR
>   - `collateralRequired` (Boolean, default: false)
>   - `subsidyPercentage` (Number, default: 0)
>   - `eligibilityCriteria` ([String])
>   - `summaryText` (String) // Clean textual summary for vector embeddings
>   - `vectorIndexId` (Number) // Position in FAISS vector store
> - **`models/Application.js`:**
>   - `userId` (ObjectId, ref: User)
>   - `schemeId` (ObjectId, ref: Scheme)
>   - `businessIdeaText` (String)
>   - `generatedApplicationText` (String)
>   - `createdAt` (Date)
> 
> #### 2. Ingestion & Vector Seeding Script (`scripts/seedSchemes.js`)
> - Connect to MongoDB.
> - Read all `.pdf` files from `./data/pdfs/`.
> - Use `pdf-parse` to extract text from each PDF.
> - Send text to Gemini API to parse structured JSON fields matching `Scheme.js`.
> - Initialize `faiss-node` IndexFlatL2 (dimension: 768).
> - Generate embeddings for each scheme's `summaryText` using Gemini `text-embedding-004`.
> - Insert vectors into FAISS and store schemes in MongoDB with `vectorIndexId`.
> - Save FAISS binary index to `./data/vectors/scheme_index.bin` and mapping to `./data/vectors/id_mapping.json`.
> 
> #### 3. Hybrid RAG Search Utility (`utils/schemeMatcher.js`)
> Function `matchSchemesForIdea(businessIdeaText, isWomanEntrepreneur = true)`:
> - Pre-filter MongoDB for schemes where `minWomenOwnership` $\le$ (51 if `isWomanEntrepreneur` else 0).
> - Convert `businessIdeaText` into vector using Gemini `text-embedding-004`.
> - Query `./data/vectors/scheme_index.bin` with `faiss-node` for top K matches.
> - Fetch matched scheme documents from MongoDB.
> - Pass scheme context and idea to Gemini to format Pros (✅) and Cons (❌) specific to the user's business idea.
> 
> #### 4. Loan Application Generator Endpoint (`controllers/schemeController.js`)
> - **`POST /api/schemes/scan`:** Executes `matchSchemesForIdea` and returns matched schemes array.
> - **`POST /api/schemes/generate-application`:** Takes `schemeId` and `businessIdeaText`, formats a formal bank loan application addressed to the Branch Manager emphasizing CGTMSE/Mudra credit guarantees, and saves it in `models/Application.js`.
> 
> #### 5. Frontend UI Components (React + Tailwind CSS)
> - **`IdeaInput.jsx`:** Textarea for idea description + "Scan Schemes 🚀" button with active loading state.
> - **`SchemeCards.jsx`:** Displays 3+ scheme cards with Pros/Cons bullets and "Generate Loan Application 📄" CTA.
> - **`ApplicationModal.jsx`:** Modal displaying AI-generated loan application draft with "Save" and "Download PDF" actions.
> 
> Provide fully written, clean code across all files without placeholders.